       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day.\n- A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove those risks.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), for inflammatory conditions\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), for pain or fever\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm the indication and that you're aware it exceeds the maximum. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first. You may also want to add a note about GI protection or the planned duration."
